doc:sec-15gg-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15GG(1) ART Minister may nominate ART members" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister administering the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 (the ART Minister) may, by writing, nominate a person who holds one of the following appointments to the Administrative Review Tribunal to deal with applications under subsection 15GU(1) (which deals with extending authorities for controlled operations beyond 3 months):  (a) Deputy President;  (b) a senior member;  (c) a general member." ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GG(2) ART Minister may nominate ART members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15gg-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Despite subsection (1), the ART Minister must not nominate a person who holds an appointment as a senior member appointed on a sessional basis or a general member of the Tribunal unless the person:  (a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of another federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of the Australian Capital Territory; and  (b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Despite subsection (1), the ART Minister must not nominate a person who holds an appointment as a senior member appointed on a sessional basis or a general member of the Tribunal unless the person:  (a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of another federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of the Australian Capital Territory; and  (b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4c8545ba40820eff780ffe7156cf741d40354e8bac41b79371ab7af7f97468b4" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must not nominate a person without being enrolled as a legal practitioner for at least 5 years." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
