doc:sec-15gh-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15GH(3) Applications for authorities to conduct controlled operations" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Nothing in this Part prevents an application for an authority being made in respect of a controlled operation that has been the subject of a previous application, but in that case the subsequent application must be a formal application. Note: An urgent authority can be varied, but not so as to extend its duration—see sections 15GO and 15GS." ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GH(4) Applications for authorities to conduct controlled operations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15gh-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) An application (whether formal or urgent) must:  (a) provide sufficient information to enable the authorising officer to decide whether or not to grant the application; and  (b) state whether or not the proposed controlled operation, or any other controlled operation with respect to the same criminal activity, has been the subject of an earlier application (whether formal or urgent) for an authority or variation of an authority and, if so, whether or not the authority was given or the variation granted; and   Controlled operations  Part IAB Authorisation of controlled operations  Division 2  Section 15GI  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) state the proposed period of effect of the authority, which must not exceed:  (i) in the case of a formal application—3 months; and  (ii) in the case of an urgent application—7 days." ;
    skos:definition "(4) An application (whether formal or urgent) must:  (a) provide sufficient information to enable the authorising officer to decide whether or not to grant the application; and  (b) state whether or not the proposed controlled operation, or any other controlled operation with respect to the same criminal activity, has been the subject of an earlier application (whether formal or urgent) for an authority or variation of an authority and, if so, whether or not the authority was given or the variation granted; and   Controlled operations  Part IAB Authorisation of controlled operations  Division 2  Section 15GI  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) state the proposed period of effect of the authority, which must not exceed:  (i) in the case of a formal application—3 months; and  (ii) in the case of an urgent application—7 days."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7cafbf62f272c9931f684daf8514141465d9b43e243df9f207178829ffb72c90" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Application requirements for controlled operations" ;
    dc:description "sufficient information, earlier application details, proposed period of effect" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
