doc:sec-15gi-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15GI(1) Determination of applications" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) An authorising officer may, after considering an application for an authority to conduct a controlled operation, and any additional information provided under subsection 15GH(5):  (a) authorise the controlled operation by granting the authority, either unconditionally or subject to conditions; or  (b) refuse the application." ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gi-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GI(2) Determination of applications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15gi-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) An authorising officer must not grant an authority to conduct a controlled operation unless the authorising officer is satisfied on reasonable grounds:  (a) that either:  (i) a serious Commonwealth offence or a serious State offence that has a federal aspect has been, is being or is likely to be committed; or  (ii) an integrity testing authority is in effect in relation to an offence that it is suspected has been, is being or is likely to be committed by a staff member of a target agency (see the notes at the foot of this subsection); and  (b) that the nature and extent of the suspected criminal activity are such as to justify the conduct of a controlled operation; and   Part IAB  Controlled operations" ;
    skos:definition "(2) An authorising officer must not grant an authority to conduct a controlled operation unless the authorising officer is satisfied on reasonable grounds:  (a) that either:  (i) a serious Commonwealth offence or a serious State offence that has a federal aspect has been, is being or is likely to be committed; or  (ii) an integrity testing authority is in effect in relation to an offence that it is suspected has been, is being or is likely to be committed by a staff member of a target agency (see the notes at the foot of this subsection); and  (b) that the nature and extent of the suspected criminal activity are such as to justify the conduct of a controlled operation; and   Part IAB  Controlled operations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "191aa6930a7348dc16ba1205119275ec276f53981dca1695af987a291821f805" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gi ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorising officer must not grant authority to conduct controlled operation without reasonable grounds" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
