doc:sec-15gi-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15GI(2) Determination of applications" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An authorising officer must not grant an authority to conduct a controlled operation unless the authorising officer is satisfied on reasonable grounds:  (a) that either:  (i) a serious Commonwealth offence or a serious State offence that has a federal aspect has been, is being or is likely to be committed; or  (ii) an integrity testing authority is in effect in relation to an offence that it is suspected has been, is being or is likely to be committed by a staff member of a target agency (see the notes at the foot of this subsection); and  (b) that the nature and extent of the suspected criminal activity are such as to justify the conduct of a controlled operation; and   Part IAB  Controlled operations" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gj a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GJ Manner of granting authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15gj ;
    values:originalText "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted:  (a) in the case of a formal application (other than a formal application referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of a written document, signed by the authorising officer (such an authority is a formal authority); or  (b) in the case of:  (i) an urgent application; or  (ii) a formal application, if the authorising officer is satisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal authority may affect the success of the controlled operation;   Part IAB  Controlled operations" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted:  (a) in the case of a formal application (other than a formal application referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of a written document, signed by the authorising officer (such an authority is a formal authority); or  (b) in the case of:  (i) an urgent application; or  (ii) a formal application, if the authorising officer is satisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal authority may affect the success of the controlled operation;   Part IAB  Controlled operations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e1ca7a1986c07deb386ec81ada181976b585e16ccb5bf77569172f10113ed679" ;
    cof:pageNumber "33"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authority to conduct controlled operation may be granted by written document or formal application with authorising officer's satisfaction." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.33" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gj-norm .
