doc:sec-15gp-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15GP(3) Application to appropriate authorising officer" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) An application for the variation may be made:  (a) by means of a written document that is signed by the applicant (such an application is a formal variation application); or  (b) if the applicant has reason to believe that the delay caused by making a formal variation application may affect the success of the controlled operation to which the authority relates— orally in person, or by telephone or any other means of communication (such an application is an urgent variation application)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gp-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GP(4) Application to appropriate authorising officer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15gp-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) More than one application for a variation under this section may be made in respect of the same authority. However, if an urgent variation of authority was granted as a result of an application under this section, the next application must be a formal variation application.   Part IAB  Controlled operations" ;
    skos:definition "(4) More than one application for a variation under this section may be made in respect of the same authority. However, if an urgent variation of authority was granted as a result of an application under this section, the next application must be a formal variation application.   Part IAB  Controlled operations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8c9f3fed6c38fa7af51a8f03488da13408fd9cc5c7e27dd46db62e236aea943e" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gp ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Multiple applications for variation under section 15GP(4) are allowed." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.39" ;
