concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gs a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GS Form of variation of authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15gs ;
    values:originalText "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer (whether formal or urgent) must:  (a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority relates; and  (b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the authority; and  (c) if the authority was varied on an application made under section 15GP, state:  (i) the name of the applicant; and  (ii) whether the application was a formal variation application or an urgent variation application; and  (d) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or was granted; and  (e) describe the variation having regard to the matters referred to in subsection 15GO(2); and  (f) if the variation extends the period of effect of a formal authority—state the period of the extension.  (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension must not exceed:  (a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions); and  (b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:  (i) 7 days; and  (ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions).   Controlled operations  Part IAB Authorisation of controlled operations  Division 2  Section 15GT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Subdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated Tribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer (whether formal or urgent) must:  (a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority relates; and  (b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the authority; and  (c) if the authority was varied on an application made under section 15GP, state:  (i) the name of the applicant; and  (ii) whether the application was a formal variation application or an urgent variation application; and  (d) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or was granted; and  (e) describe the variation having regard to the matters referred to in subsection 15GO(2); and  (f) if the variation extends the period of effect of a formal authority—state the period of the extension.  (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension must not exceed:  (a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions); and  (b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:  (i) 7 days; and  (ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions).   Controlled operations  Part IAB Authorisation of controlled operations  Division 2  Section 15GT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Subdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated Tribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3e7059a133d10d09659a9153fe66eae4335b1d9b7e270fc384bc8b0b26926d7f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gs-ss-1 ;
