doc:sec-15gs-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15GS(1) Form of variation of authority" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer (whether formal or urgent) must:  (a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority relates; and  (b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the authority; and  (c) if the authority was varied on an application made under section 15GP, state:  (i) the name of the applicant; and  (ii) whether the application was a formal variation application or an urgent variation application; and  (d) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or was granted; and  (e) describe the variation having regard to the matters referred to in subsection 15GO(2); and  (f) if the variation extends the period of effect of a formal authority—state the period of the extension." ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gs-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15GS(2) Form of variation of authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15gs-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension must not exceed:  (a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions); and  (b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:  (i) 7 days; and  (ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions).   Controlled operations  Part IAB Authorisation of controlled operations  Division 2  Section 15GT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Subdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated Tribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months" ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension must not exceed:  (a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions); and  (b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:  (i) 7 days; and  (ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding 3 months (including any previous extensions).   Controlled operations  Part IAB Authorisation of controlled operations  Division 2  Section 15GT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Subdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated Tribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "96802a2eef2038f2c58ec402c6dffd1107c2f24c9902e29faf1091e968d2262c" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gs ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Maximum period for extension of authority beyond 3 months" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
