concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jk a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15JK Integrity testing authorities—variation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15jk ;
    values:originalText "(1) An appropriate authorising officer for an integrity testing operation that is authorised by an integrity testing authority may, in writing, vary the authority:  (a) at any time on the authorising officer’s own initiative; or  (b) on application, in writing, by the responsible staff member for the operation.  (2) A variation may extend, or further extend, the period of effect of the authority for up to 12 months, but not so that the period of effect ends more than 24 months after the authority was granted.  (3) As soon as practicable after varying an integrity testing authority for an integrity testing operation, the authorising officer must give a copy of the variation to:   Part IABA  Integrity testing" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An appropriate authorising officer for an integrity testing operation that is authorised by an integrity testing authority may, in writing, vary the authority:  (a) at any time on the authorising officer’s own initiative; or  (b) on application, in writing, by the responsible staff member for the operation.  (2) A variation may extend, or further extend, the period of effect of the authority for up to 12 months, but not so that the period of effect ends more than 24 months after the authority was granted.  (3) As soon as practicable after varying an integrity testing authority for an integrity testing operation, the authorising officer must give a copy of the variation to:   Part IABA  Integrity testing"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "407679336fd7c11c73889398cfc798cc47a27c31250169987e33ff74d02684db" ;
    cof:pageNumber "93"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jk-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jk-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jk-ss-3 ;
