concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm cml:asserts concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm-logic-deontic-1 .
concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm-logic-deontic-1 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Implies" ;
    cml:logicSummary "If a defect affects the application, authority or variation in a material particular, then the application is invalidated." ;
    cml:premiseText "defect(a) ∧ (a = application ∨ a = authority ∨ a = variation)" ;
    cml:conclusionText "(a = application ∨ a = authority ∨ a = variation) → ¬(application is invalidated by defect(a))" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "0.5000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-15jm a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15JM Integrity testing authorities—defects" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "An application for an integrity testing authority or for the variation of an authority, and any integrity testing authority or variation granted on the basis of such an application, is not invalidated by any defect, other than a defect that affects the application, authority or variation in a material particular.   Integrity testing  Part IABA Integrity testing operations: protection of participants  Division 3  Section 15JN  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jn a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15JN Integrity testing operations—authorised conduct"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15jn ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an integrity testing authority for an integrity testing operation authorises each person identified in the authority as a participant to take part in the operation, subject to any conditions set out in the authority. Note: Paragraphs 15JH(1)(d) and (e) require participants to be identified, and the nature of the operation to be described, in the authority. Subsection 15JH(2), however, allows for participants to be identified in the authority by an assumed identity, or by code.  (2) A participant is authorised to take part in the integrity testing operation for the period of effect of the authority, unless:  (a) the authority states (or is varied to state) a shorter period during which the person is so authorised; or  (b) the authority is varied to provide that the person is no longer so authorised; or  (c) the authority is cancelled before the end of that period.  (3) An integrity testing authority does not authorise a participant identified in the authority to delegate participation to another person." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an integrity testing authority for an integrity testing operation authorises each person identified in the authority as a participant to take part in the operation, subject to any conditions set out in the authority. Note: Paragraphs 15JH(1)(d) and (e) require participants to be identified, and the nature of the operation to be described, in the authority. Subsection 15JH(2), however, allows for participants to be identified in the authority by an assumed identity, or by code.  (2) A participant is authorised to take part in the integrity testing operation for the period of effect of the authority, unless:  (a) the authority states (or is varied to state) a shorter period during which the person is so authorised; or  (b) the authority is varied to provide that the person is no longer so authorised; or  (c) the authority is cancelled before the end of that period.  (3) An integrity testing authority does not authorise a participant identified in the authority to delegate participation to another person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2a087db36becac2683460fca99848b5b742a0cffa4c78f2bda2f859d7743c4a2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "95"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jn-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jn-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jn-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.95" .
doc:sec-15jn a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15JN Integrity testing operations—authorised conduct" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an integrity testing authority for an integrity testing operation authorises each person identified in the authority as a participant to take part in the operation, subject to any conditions set out in the authority. Note: Paragraphs 15JH(1)(d) and (e) require participants to be identified, and the nature of the operation to be described, in the authority. Subsection 15JH(2), however, allows for participants to be identified in the authority by an assumed identity, or by code.  (2) A participant is authorised to take part in the integrity testing operation for the period of effect of the authority, unless:  (a) the authority states (or is varied to state) a shorter period during which the person is so authorised; or  (b) the authority is varied to provide that the person is no longer so authorised; or  (c) the authority is cancelled before the end of that period.  (3) An integrity testing authority does not authorise a participant identified in the authority to delegate participation to another person." ;
    cof:pageNumber "95"^^xsd:integer .

