concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jq-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15JQ(4) Integrity testing operations—disclosure"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15jq-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person discloses the information to an IGIS official for the purpose of the IGIS official exercising a power, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official. Note: A defendant, except for an IGIS official, bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in this subsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code). For IGIS officials, see section 34C of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986." ;
    skos:definition "(4) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person discloses the information to an IGIS official for the purpose of the IGIS official exercising a power, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official. Note: A defendant, except for an IGIS official, bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in this subsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code). For IGIS officials, see section 34C of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "672a70ed045550909e0fb1e5c7766f4564f086bbbea3917dd9bbf7d5bfcfd263" ;
