concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15KC Form of authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15kc ;
    values:originalText "(1) An authority must be:  (a) in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and  (b) signed by the person granting it.  (2) An authority must state the following:  (a) the name of the person granting the authority;  (b) the date of the authority;  (c) details of the assumed identity authorised;  (d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be acquired under the authority;  (e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;  (f) why the authority is granted;   Part IAC  Assumed Identities" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An authority must be:  (a) in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and  (b) signed by the person granting it.  (2) An authority must state the following:  (a) the name of the person granting the authority;  (b) the date of the authority;  (c) details of the assumed identity authorised;  (d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be acquired under the authority;  (e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;  (f) why the authority is granted;   Part IAC  Assumed Identities"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e6a584a43c7f5e62215052639a737af37e051df296ba18d7cbcbc51e2d66b7bc" ;
