concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kl a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15KL Cancellation of evidence of assumed identity"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15kl ;
    values:originalText "(1) The chief officer of an issuing agency who produces evidence of an assumed identity under this Part must cancel the evidence if directed in writing to do so by the chief officer who requested the evidence. Note 1: The chief officer who requested the evidence may delegate functions under this section—see section 15LH.   Part IAC  Assumed Identities" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The chief officer of an issuing agency who produces evidence of an assumed identity under this Part must cancel the evidence if directed in writing to do so by the chief officer who requested the evidence. Note 1: The chief officer who requested the evidence may delegate functions under this section—see section 15LH.   Part IAC  Assumed Identities"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "99f99496f92c14222c54cf5eb6d65ad1edcc13c74887e4a532a23d62b5c324e5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "121"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Chief officer must cancel evidence of assumed identity upon written direction." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.121" ;
