concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15LC Disclosing information about assumed identity"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15lc ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and   Assumed Identities  Part IAC Compliance and Monitoring  Division 6  Section 15LC  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another person has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an assumed identity. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and  (c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another person has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an assumed identity; and  (d) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will endanger the health or safety of any person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and  (c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another person has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an assumed identity; and  (d) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will prejudice the effective conduct of an investigation or intelligence-gathering in relation to criminal activity. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (4) A person does not commit an offence under subsection (1), (2) or (3) if the person causes the disclosure of information mentioned in paragraph (1)(c), (2)(c) or (3)(c) (as the case may be) and the disclosure is:  (a) in connection with the administration or execution of this Part or a corresponding assumed identity law; or  (b) for the purposes of any legal proceeding arising out of or otherwise related to this Part or a corresponding assumed identity law or of any report of any such proceedings; or   Part IAC  Assumed Identities" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and   Assumed Identities  Part IAC Compliance and Monitoring  Division 6  Section 15LC  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another person has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an assumed identity. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and  (c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another person has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an assumed identity; and  (d) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will endanger the health or safety of any person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person engages in conduct; and  (b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and  (c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another person has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an assumed identity; and  (d) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will prejudice the effective conduct of an investigation or intelligence-gathering in relation to criminal activity. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (4) A person does not commit an offence under subsection (1), (2) or (3) if the person causes the disclosure of information mentioned in paragraph (1)(c), (2)(c) or (3)(c) (as the case may be) and the disclosure is:  (a) in connection with the administration or execution of this Part or a corresponding assumed identity law; or  (b) for the purposes of any legal proceeding arising out of or otherwise related to this Part or a corresponding assumed identity law or of any report of any such proceedings; or   Part IAC  Assumed Identities"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eba4b5d85613f1085f6907ca96fcbd088fc591f24e18ceae012236d1458014d4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "134"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lc-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lc-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lc-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lc-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lc-ss-3 ;
