doc:sec-15mb-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15MB(2) Meaning of civil proceeding" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) To avoid doubt, each of the following is part of a civil proceeding:  (a) any proceeding on an ex parte application (including an application made before pleadings are filed in a court);  (b) the discovery, exchange, production, inspection or disclosure of intended evidence, documents and reports of persons intended to be called by a party to give evidence;  (c) an appeal proceeding;  (d) any interlocutory or other proceeding prescribed by regulations for the purposes of this paragraph. 15MC  When a charge is outstanding or pending" ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mb-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15MB(1) Meaning of civil proceeding"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15mb-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Part:   Witness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA Preliminary  Division 1  Section 15MC  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) a charge against a person for an offence is outstanding until the charge is finally dealt with in any of the following ways:  (i) the charge is withdrawn;  (ii) the charge is dismissed by a court;  (iii) the person is discharged by a court following a committal hearing;  (iv) the person is acquitted or found guilty of the offence by a court; and  (b) a charge against a person for an offence is pending if the person has not yet been charged with the offence, but:  (i) the person has been arrested for the offence, unless the person has been later released without being charged with an offence; or  (ii) a summons to appear before a court to answer a charge for the offence has been served on the person; and  (c) an allegation of professional misconduct against a person is outstanding if the allegation has not been finally dealt with in accordance with the procedures that apply for the purposes of dealing with an allegation of that kind.   Part IACA  Witness identity protection for operatives" ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Part:   Witness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA Preliminary  Division 1  Section 15MC  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) a charge against a person for an offence is outstanding until the charge is finally dealt with in any of the following ways:  (i) the charge is withdrawn;  (ii) the charge is dismissed by a court;  (iii) the person is discharged by a court following a committal hearing;  (iv) the person is acquitted or found guilty of the offence by a court; and  (b) a charge against a person for an offence is pending if the person has not yet been charged with the offence, but:  (i) the person has been arrested for the offence, unless the person has been later released without being charged with an offence; or  (ii) a summons to appear before a court to answer a charge for the offence has been served on the person; and  (c) an allegation of professional misconduct against a person is outstanding if the allegation has not been finally dealt with in accordance with the procedures that apply for the purposes of dealing with an allegation of that kind.   Part IACA  Witness identity protection for operatives"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "34e4ecc8416c34789a32d5d462188b25a8e3e992cfa5cc72b9010dc748901ee8" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mb ;
    cof:pageNumber "146"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A charge against a person for an offence is outstanding until the charge is finally dealt with in one of the following ways. Defines civil proceeding for the purpose of this Part." ;
