concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ya-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YA(1) Definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15ya-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In a proceeding for a Commonwealth offence, the court may declare a person to be a special witness in relation to the proceeding if satisfied that the person is unlikely to be able to satisfactorily give evidence in the ordinary manner because of:  (a) a disability; or  (b) intimidation, distress or emotional trauma arising from:  (i) the person’s age, cultural background or relationship to a party to the proceeding; or  (ii) the nature of the evidence; or  (iii) some other relevant factor.   Part IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons" ;
    skos:definition "(1) In a proceeding for a Commonwealth offence, the court may declare a person to be a special witness in relation to the proceeding if satisfied that the person is unlikely to be able to satisfactorily give evidence in the ordinary manner because of:  (a) a disability; or  (b) intimidation, distress or emotional trauma arising from:  (i) the person’s age, cultural background or relationship to a party to the proceeding; or  (ii) the nature of the evidence; or  (iii) some other relevant factor.   Part IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "91952c9560ceda8c0f1719b232bb5ce88179e912574e5775aa901ef0a89d9529" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ya ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines a vulnerable adult complainant in relation to a vulnerable adult proceeding. Court may declare a person special witness if unlikely to give evidence in ordinary manner due to disability, intimidation, distress or emotional trauma." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.170" ;
