concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YD Leave under this Division"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yd ;
    values:originalText "(1) An application for leave under this Division:  (a) must be in writing; and  (b) if there is a jury in the proceeding in question—must be made in the jury’s absence; and  (c) must not be determined before the court has considered such submissions and other evidence as it thinks necessary for determining the application.  (2) If the court gives leave under this Division, the court must:  (a) state its reasons in writing; and  (b) cause those reasons to be entered in the court’s records.   Protecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD Evidence recording hearings  Division 2A  Section 15YDA  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
