    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "complainants  (1) A defendant in a child proceeding who is not represented by counsel is not to cross-examine a child complainant. Note: A person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal proceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.  (2) A person appointed by the court is to ask the child any questions that the defendant requests the person to ask the child. 15YFA  Unrepresented defendants—cross-examination of vulnerable adult complainants  (1) A defendant in a vulnerable adult proceeding who is not represented by counsel is not to cross-examine a vulnerable adult complainant.   Protecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD Cross-examination  Division 3  Section 15YG  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Note: A person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal proceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.  (2) A person appointed by the court is to ask the vulnerable adult complainant any questions that the defendant requests the person to ask the complainant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "182"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yf-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YF(1) Unrepresented defendants—cross-examination of child"@en ;
