concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yh a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YH Represented defendants—cross-examination of vulnerable"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yh ;
    values:originalText "persons  (1) A defendant in a proceeding who is represented by counsel is not to cross-examine, except through counsel, a person to whom subsection (2) applies. Note: A person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal proceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.  (2) This subsection applies to the following persons:  (a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;  (b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult complainant;  (c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom an order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this section. 15YHA  Committal proceedings—cross-examination of vulnerable persons  (1) A person is not to cross-examine, at committal proceedings or proceedings of a similar kind, a person to whom subsection (2) applies.  (2) This subsection applies to the following persons:  (a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;  (b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult complainant;   Protecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD Cross-examination  Division 3  Section 15YHA  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom an order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this section.   Part IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons" ;
    skos:definition "persons  (1) A defendant in a proceeding who is represented by counsel is not to cross-examine, except through counsel, a person to whom subsection (2) applies. Note: A person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal proceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.  (2) This subsection applies to the following persons:  (a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;  (b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult complainant;  (c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom an order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this section. 15YHA  Committal proceedings—cross-examination of vulnerable persons  (1) A person is not to cross-examine, at committal proceedings or proceedings of a similar kind, a person to whom subsection (2) applies.  (2) This subsection applies to the following persons:  (a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;  (b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult complainant;   Protecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD Cross-examination  Division 3  Section 15YHA  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom an order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this section.   Part IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d39245fa8f8a21c2dfb27b99b7eb54bc9286e35ca9f79b6ee5d8229504475d0e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "184"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yh-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yh-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yh-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yh-ss-2 ;
