concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yj-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YJ(3) Giving evidence by closed-circuit television"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yj-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The court may adjourn the proceeding, or a part of the proceeding, to a court or other place that is equipped with facilities for evidence to be given by means of closed-circuit television if:  (a) the court is not equipped with facilities for evidence to be given by means of closed-circuit television; or  (b) the court otherwise considers it appropriate to do so." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The court may adjourn the proceeding, or a part of the proceeding, to a court or other place that is equipped with facilities for evidence to be given by means of closed-circuit television if:  (a) the court is not equipped with facilities for evidence to be given by means of closed-circuit television; or  (b) the court otherwise considers it appropriate to do so."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0a23d8793809bbb2c979c17537858b500b6ca9d3a69c3d600b3acc83cb4718d8" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yj ;
