concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yl-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YL(1) Alternative arrangements for giving evidence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yl-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to whom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if:  (a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in another proceeding; and   Protecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD Special facilities for vulnerable persons to give evidence  Division 4  Section 15YLA  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and  (c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to whom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if:  (a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in another proceeding; and   Protecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD Special facilities for vulnerable persons to give evidence  Division 4  Section 15YLA  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and  (c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d21033b356ee53994b99b40b58e3b1263ff304cd182d9a1a25472f15826ccd24" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yl ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court must order recording of evidence given by vulnerable persons under certain conditions. Court must make arrangements to restrict contact with defendant and public while giving evidence." ;
