    cof:pageNumber "197"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ys a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YS General powers of a court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15ys ;
    values:originalText "(1) The power of a court to control the conduct of a proceeding is not affected by this Part, except so far as this Part provides otherwise expressly or by necessary intendment.  (2) In particular, the powers of a court to control the questioning of witnesses are not affected.   Protecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD Miscellaneous  Division 6  Section 15YT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (3) The power of a court to give leave under this Part includes the power to give such leave subject to conditions." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The power of a court to control the conduct of a proceeding is not affected by this Part, except so far as this Part provides otherwise expressly or by necessary intendment.  (2) In particular, the powers of a court to control the questioning of witnesses are not affected.   Protecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD Miscellaneous  Division 6  Section 15YT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (3) The power of a court to give leave under this Part includes the power to give such leave subject to conditions."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "dd0221e918cd9fe31f230e25dd895cc31012f46075b2aa92a1ea7d5256519a5b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "200"^^xsd:integer ;
