doc:sec-15yu-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15YU(5) Proceedings to which this Part applies" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) In this section:   Part IAE  Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Section 15YV  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  PMV-related questioning warrant means a questioning warrant that is issued in relation to politically motivated violence (within the meaning of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979). questioning warrant has the same meaning as in Division 3 of Part III of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979. 15YV  When court may take evidence by video link Application by prosecutor" ;
    cof:pageNumber "202"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YU(1) Proceedings to which this Part applies"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yu-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In a proceeding, the court must:  (a) direct; or  (b) by order, allow; a witness to give evidence by video link if:  (c) both:  (i) the prosecutor applies for the direction or order; and  (ii) the court is satisfied that the prosecutor gave the court reasonable notice of his or her intention to make the application; and  (d) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and  (e) the witness is available, or will reasonably be available, to give evidence by video link; and  (f) the facilities required by section 15YY are available or can reasonably be made available; unless the court is satisfied that giving the direction or making the order would have a substantial adverse effect on the right of a defendant in the proceeding to receive a fair hearing. Application by defendant" ;
    skos:definition "(1) In a proceeding, the court must:  (a) direct; or  (b) by order, allow; a witness to give evidence by video link if:  (c) both:  (i) the prosecutor applies for the direction or order; and  (ii) the court is satisfied that the prosecutor gave the court reasonable notice of his or her intention to make the application; and  (d) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and  (e) the witness is available, or will reasonably be available, to give evidence by video link; and  (f) the facilities required by section 15YY are available or can reasonably be made available; unless the court is satisfied that giving the direction or making the order would have a substantial adverse effect on the right of a defendant in the proceeding to receive a fair hearing. Application by defendant"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "62780883560f883efee960534844eeb45707af9543e5e9857dd9db0474e1d64c" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu ;
    cof:pageNumber "202"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court must allow witness to give evidence by video link under certain conditions. Proceedings for specified offences apply to this Part." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
