concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yy a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YY Technical requirements for video link"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yy ;
    values:originalText "(1) A witness can give evidence under a section 15YV direction or order only if:  (a) the courtroom or other place where the court is sitting (the courtroom point); and  (b) the place where the evidence is given (the witness point); are equipped with video facilities that:  (c) enable appropriate persons at the courtroom point to see and hear the witness give the evidence; and  (d) enable appropriate persons at the witness point to see and hear appropriate persons at the courtroom point.  (2) In subsection (1): appropriate persons means such persons as the court considers appropriate." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A witness can give evidence under a section 15YV direction or order only if:  (a) the courtroom or other place where the court is sitting (the courtroom point); and  (b) the place where the evidence is given (the witness point); are equipped with video facilities that:  (c) enable appropriate persons at the courtroom point to see and hear the witness give the evidence; and  (d) enable appropriate persons at the witness point to see and hear appropriate persons at the courtroom point.  (2) In subsection (1): appropriate persons means such persons as the court considers appropriate."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9280a0b4abf7dde1a84ace364270f24e4df7fec7f416429fb41ff13c457b65df" ;
    cof:pageNumber "209"^^xsd:integer ;
