    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yz-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a proceeding involves a jury; and  (b) a witness gives evidence under a section 15YV direction or order; and  (c) the evidence is admissible in the proceeding; the judge must give the jury such direction as the judge thinks necessary to ensure that the jury gives the same weight to the evidence as if it had been given by the witness in the courtroom or other place where the court is sitting." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a proceeding involves a jury; and  (b) a witness gives evidence under a section 15YV direction or order; and  (c) the evidence is admissible in the proceeding; the judge must give the jury such direction as the judge thinks necessary to ensure that the jury gives the same weight to the evidence as if it had been given by the witness in the courtroom or other place where the court is sitting."@en ;
