concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yz-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YZ(1) Direction to jury"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yz-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a court gives a section 15YV direction or makes a section 15YV order; and  (b) the prosecutor applied for the direction or order;   Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Part IAE  Section 15YZE  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  a defendant in the proceeding may appeal against the direction or order." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a court gives a section 15YV direction or makes a section 15YV order; and  (b) the prosecutor applied for the direction or order;   Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Part IAE  Section 15YZE  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  a defendant in the proceeding may appeal against the direction or order."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "079ea53ed8c3c460cb22e17596301823a7ee8f92e34a5cfb790e9e1018d6da03" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yz ;
    cof:pageNumber "209"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defendant may appeal against section 15YV direction or order. Ensure equal weight to witness evidence in jury proceedings. A person must give evidence at the courtroom or other place where the court is sitting." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
