concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yz-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15YZ(5) Direction to jury"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15yz-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A court that has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a judgment, order or direction in the proceeding has jurisdiction to hear and determine any appeal under this section. 15YZE  Other laws about evidence not affected  This Part does not prevent any other law about taking evidence of a witness from applying for the purposes of a proceeding.   Part IAE  Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Section 15YZF  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  15YZF  Saving of other laws  This Part is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any other law of the Commonwealth or any law of a State or Territory.   Sentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB Interpretation  Division 1  Section 16  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(5) A court that has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a judgment, order or direction in the proceeding has jurisdiction to hear and determine any appeal under this section. 15YZE  Other laws about evidence not affected  This Part does not prevent any other law about taking evidence of a witness from applying for the purposes of a proceeding.   Part IAE  Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Section 15YZF  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  15YZF  Saving of other laws  This Part is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any other law of the Commonwealth or any law of a State or Territory.   Sentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB Interpretation  Division 1  Section 16  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fbd5cd53472030c77538d38c39e06aeadc881f6fc5e261735f725259e775c8f0" ;
