doc:sec-16ab-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "16AB(6) Matters relating to victim impact statements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) The person convicted of the offence may only test the facts in a victim impact statement:  (a) by way of cross-examining the maker of the statement; and  (b) if the court gives leave to do so." ;
    cof:pageNumber "230"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-16ab-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16AB(7) Matters relating to victim impact statements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-16ab-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) For the purposes of Part IAD (about protecting vulnerable persons):  (a) giving evidence includes giving a reading under subsection (4); and  (b) a cross-examination includes a cross-examination under subsection (6). Note: This confirms that any protections available under Part IAD will be available for the reading or the cross-examination." ;
    skos:definition "(7) For the purposes of Part IAD (about protecting vulnerable persons):  (a) giving evidence includes giving a reading under subsection (4); and  (b) a cross-examination includes a cross-examination under subsection (6). Note: This confirms that any protections available under Part IAD will be available for the reading or the cross-examination."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1b3152e3f538f0f421f056c56135614c988e04bc5a67797a368666815ab70bc5" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-16ab ;
    cof:pageNumber "230"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Part IAD protections apply to readings and cross-examinations." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
