    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person is convicted of one or more section 17B offences relating to property, money or both, whose total value is not more than $2,000; and  (b) the person has not previously been sentenced to imprisonment for any federal, State or Territory offence; the court convicting the person is not to pass a sentence of imprisonment for that offence, or for any of those offences, unless the court is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person is convicted of one or more section 17B offences relating to property, money or both, whose total value is not more than $2,000; and  (b) the person has not previously been sentenced to imprisonment for any federal, State or Territory offence; the court convicting the person is not to pass a sentence of imprisonment for that offence, or for any of those offences, unless the court is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that warrant it."@en ;
