doc:sec-19ar-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "19AR(4) Fixing of non-parole period etc. where parole or licence taken" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) A court may decline to fix a non-parole period if:  (a) the court is satisfied that doing so is appropriate, having regard to:  (i) the serious nature and circumstances of the offence or offences; and  (ii) the antecedents of the person; or  (b) the person is expected to be serving a State or Territory sentence on the day after the end of the federal sentence, or the last to be served of the federal sentences." ;
    cof:pageNumber "266"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19as a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "19AS Court to issue warrant of detention where person required to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-19as ;
    values:originalText "serve balance of sentence  (1) If:  (a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or federal sentences is released on parole or licence under this Act; and  (b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences) to a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more federal, State or Territory offences committed during the parole period or licence period; and  (c) under section 19AQ:  (i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been revoked; and  (ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence or sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences); then:  (d) the court imposing the new sentence or sentences must issue a warrant authorising the person to be detained in prison to   Sentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB Conditional release on parole or licence  Division 5  Section 19AT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  undergo imprisonment for the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or sentences; and  (e) the person must begin to serve the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or of the first to be served of the outstanding sentences on the day that the new sentence is, or the new sentences are, imposed; and  (f) the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or of each of the outstanding sentences must be served in the State or Territory where the new sentence is, or the new sentences are, imposed.  (2) Where the court fails to issue a warrant under paragraph (1)(d), the Director of Public Prosecutions may apply to that court for such a warrant." ;
    skos:definition "serve balance of sentence  (1) If:  (a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or federal sentences is released on parole or licence under this Act; and  (b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences) to a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more federal, State or Territory offences committed during the parole period or licence period; and  (c) under section 19AQ:  (i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been revoked; and  (ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence or sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences); then:  (d) the court imposing the new sentence or sentences must issue a warrant authorising the person to be detained in prison to   Sentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB Conditional release on parole or licence  Division 5  Section 19AT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  undergo imprisonment for the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or sentences; and  (e) the person must begin to serve the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or of the first to be served of the outstanding sentences on the day that the new sentence is, or the new sentences are, imposed; and  (f) the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or of each of the outstanding sentences must be served in the State or Territory where the new sentence is, or the new sentences are, imposed.  (2) Where the court fails to issue a warrant under paragraph (1)(d), the Director of Public Prosecutions may apply to that court for such a warrant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "692fd2655ffa1eb65a0fb5882d67c40c5b933d3e255bb5d5f413ae094f22f117" ;
    cof:pageNumber "268"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19as-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19as-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
