    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A prescribed authority exercising any powers under this Division may take evidence on oath or affirmation and for that purpose may administer an oath or affirmation.  (2) A prescribed authority exercising any powers under this Division may summon a person to appear before the prescribed authority to give evidence and to produce such documents and articles (if any) as are referred to in the summons.  (3) A summons under this section shall be served in the same manner as a summons to a witness to appear before a court of summary jurisdiction in the State or Territory where the summons under this section is issued. 19AZA  Disobedience of summons etc.  (1) A person who has been served with a summons to appear before a prescribed authority must not fail to appear in obedience to the summons. Penalty: 10 penalty units.  (2) A person who has been served with a summons to produce a document or article to a prescribed authority shall not fail to produce the document or article. Penalty: 10 penalty units.  (3) A person who appears before a prescribed authority shall not refuse to be sworn or make an affirmation or refuse to produce documents or articles, or to answer questions, that he or she is required by the prescribed authority to produce or answer. Penalty: 10 penalty units.  (4) Subsections (1), (2) and (3) do not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse." ;
    cof:pageNumber "277"^^xsd:integer .

