concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20A Failure to comply with condition of discharge or release"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20a ;
    values:originalText "(1) Where a person has been discharged in pursuance of an order made under subsection 19B(1), or released in pursuance of an order made under subsection 20(1), and information is laid before a magistrate alleging that the person has, without reasonable cause or excuse, failed to comply with a condition of the order, the magistrate may:  (a) issue a summons directing the person to appear, on a date, at a time and at a place fixed in the summons, before the court by which the order was made; or  (b) if the information is laid on oath and the magistrate is of the opinion that proceedings against the person by summons" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Where a person has been discharged in pursuance of an order made under subsection 19B(1), or released in pursuance of an order made under subsection 20(1), and information is laid before a magistrate alleging that the person has, without reasonable cause or excuse, failed to comply with a condition of the order, the magistrate may:  (a) issue a summons directing the person to appear, on a date, at a time and at a place fixed in the summons, before the court by which the order was made; or  (b) if the information is laid on oath and the magistrate is of the opinion that proceedings against the person by summons"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d662564e36d96ffcc0b54719eb4c1aa814693dd664596840e178fa559bf05f4a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "285"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Failure to comply with condition of discharge or release obligation" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
