concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20aa-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20AA(6) Power to discharge or vary conditions of recognizance"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20aa-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Where an application is made under subsection (1) by a person other than an authorized person, the person making the application shall cause notice of the application, and of the date, time and place fixed for the hearing of the application, to be served on the Director of Public Prosecutions or, if the Director of Public Prosecutions has not established an office in the State or Territory in which the application is made, on the Director of Legal Services, in that State or Territory, in the Attorney-General’s Department, and:  (a) if the application is made by the person who entered into the recognizance and that person has a surety—on the surety;  (b) if the application is made by a surety in respect of the recognizance—on the person who entered into the recognizance; or  (c) if the application is made by a probation officer in respect of the recognizance—on the person who entered into the" ;
    skos:definition "(6) Where an application is made under subsection (1) by a person other than an authorized person, the person making the application shall cause notice of the application, and of the date, time and place fixed for the hearing of the application, to be served on the Director of Public Prosecutions or, if the Director of Public Prosecutions has not established an office in the State or Territory in which the application is made, on the Director of Legal Services, in that State or Territory, in the Attorney-General’s Department, and:  (a) if the application is made by the person who entered into the recognizance and that person has a surety—on the surety;  (b) if the application is made by a surety in respect of the recognizance—on the person who entered into the recognizance; or  (c) if the application is made by a probation officer in respect of the recognizance—on the person who entered into the"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d541655d3422fdacab74de1d83f9c7230ad10d3564db7984cac27d5bf99a7938" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20aa ;
    cof:pageNumber "290"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notice must be served on the Director of Public Prosecutions or Director of Legal Services in a specific manner." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
