concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20ab a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20AB Additional sentencing alternatives"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20ab ;
    values:originalText "(1) A court may pass a sentence, or make an order, in respect of a person convicted before the court in a participating State or participating Territory of a federal offence, if:  (a) subsection (1AA) applies to the sentence or order; and  (b) under the law of the State or Territory, a court is empowered to pass such a sentence, or make such an order, in respect of a State or Territory offender in corresponding cases; and  (c) the first-mentioned court is:  (i) empowered as mentioned in paragraph (b); or  (ii) a federal court.  (1AA) This subsection applies to a sentence or order that is:  (a) known as any of the following:  (i) an attendance centre order or attendance order;  (ii) a community based order;  (iii) a community correction order;  (iv) a community custody order;  (v) a community service order;  (vi) a community work order;  (vii) a drug or alcohol treatment order or rehabilitation order;" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A court may pass a sentence, or make an order, in respect of a person convicted before the court in a participating State or participating Territory of a federal offence, if:  (a) subsection (1AA) applies to the sentence or order; and  (b) under the law of the State or Territory, a court is empowered to pass such a sentence, or make such an order, in respect of a State or Territory offender in corresponding cases; and  (c) the first-mentioned court is:  (i) empowered as mentioned in paragraph (b); or  (ii) a federal court.  (1AA) This subsection applies to a sentence or order that is:  (a) known as any of the following:  (i) an attendance centre order or attendance order;  (ii) a community based order;  (iii) a community correction order;  (iv) a community custody order;  (v) a community service order;  (vi) a community work order;  (vii) a drug or alcohol treatment order or rehabilitation order;"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3dd7b068a9d4b34cc69769650d8fdca92ec7033b6664a3f3a208bd85a55b8ffc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "293"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may pass sentence or make order in respect of federal offence if certain conditions are met." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.293" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20ab-norm .
