concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20ac-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20AC(6) Failure to comply with sentence passed, or order made, under"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20ac-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Where, in accordance with this section, a person in respect of whom a sentence has been passed, or an order has been made, under subsection 20AB(1) appears or is brought before the court by which the sentence was passed or the order was made, the court (whether or not constituted by the judge or magistrate who passed the sentence or made the order), if it is satisfied that the person has, without reasonable cause or excuse, failed to comply with the sentence or order or with any requirements made in relation to the sentence or order by or under the applied provisions, may:  (a) without prejudice to the continuance of the sentence or order, impose a pecuniary penalty not exceeding 10 penalty units on the person;  (b) revoke the sentence or order and, subject to subsection (7), deal with the person, for the offence in respect of which the" ;
    skos:definition "(6) Where, in accordance with this section, a person in respect of whom a sentence has been passed, or an order has been made, under subsection 20AB(1) appears or is brought before the court by which the sentence was passed or the order was made, the court (whether or not constituted by the judge or magistrate who passed the sentence or made the order), if it is satisfied that the person has, without reasonable cause or excuse, failed to comply with the sentence or order or with any requirements made in relation to the sentence or order by or under the applied provisions, may:  (a) without prejudice to the continuance of the sentence or order, impose a pecuniary penalty not exceeding 10 penalty units on the person;  (b) revoke the sentence or order and, subject to subsection (7), deal with the person, for the offence in respect of which the"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c1485e1a3601c00e8fb890a842dbb96972919469386f117db63ce8d05d3da777" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20ac ;
    cof:pageNumber "296"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Failure to comply with sentence or order may impose a pecuniary penalty." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
