doc:sec-20b-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20B(6) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) For the purposes of subsection (3), a prima facie case is established if there is evidence that would (except for the circumstances by reason of which the person is unfit to be tried) provide sufficient grounds to put the person on trial in relation to the offence." ;
    cof:pageNumber "300"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20B(7) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20b-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) In proceedings to determine whether, for the purposes of subsection (3), a prima facie case has been established:  (a) the person may give evidence or make an unsworn statement; and  (b) the person may raise any defence that could properly be raised if the proceedings were a trial for that offence; and  (c) the court may seek such other evidence, whether oral or in writing, as it considers likely to assist in determining the matter." ;
    skos:definition "(7) In proceedings to determine whether, for the purposes of subsection (3), a prima facie case has been established:  (a) the person may give evidence or make an unsworn statement; and  (b) the person may raise any defence that could properly be raised if the proceedings were a trial for that offence; and  (c) the court may seek such other evidence, whether oral or in writing, as it considers likely to assist in determining the matter."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "98f224fc7383643e13950a5c50e988a49fb2b0f962fc2defdb9a127d997bf1de" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b ;
    cof:pageNumber "300"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Person may give evidence or make an unsworn statement in proceedings." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
