concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20BM Release order may be revoked"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20bm ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may, by instrument in writing, revoke an order made under subsection 20BL(1) (in this section called a release order) at any time while that release order remains in force:  (a) if the person concerned has, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with a condition of the order; or  (b) if there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the person has, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, so to comply;" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Attorney-General may, by instrument in writing, revoke an order made under subsection 20BL(1) (in this section called a release order) at any time while that release order remains in force:  (a) if the person concerned has, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with a condition of the order; or  (b) if there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the person has, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, so to comply;"@en ;
