doc:sec-20bm a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20BM Release order may be revoked" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may, by instrument in writing, revoke an order made under subsection 20BL(1) (in this section called a release order) at any time while that release order remains in force:  (a) if the person concerned has, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, to comply with a condition of the order; or  (b) if there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the person has, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, so to comply;" ;
    cof:pageNumber "315"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bn a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20BN Attorney-General to review detention of persons taken back"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20bn ;
    values:originalText "into detention  (1) Where, under subsection 20BM(5), a prescribed authority directs that a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the Attorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so detained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration) whether or not the person should be released from detention and must, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least once in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.  (2) Subsection 20BK(2) and, subject to the modification in subsection (3), section 20BL, apply in relation to an initial consideration and a reconsideration under subsection (1).  (3) For the purposes of applying section 20BL, subsection 20BL(1) has effect as if the reference in that subsection to subsection 20BK(1) were a reference to subsection (1) of this section." ;
    skos:definition "into detention  (1) Where, under subsection 20BM(5), a prescribed authority directs that a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the Attorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so detained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration) whether or not the person should be released from detention and must, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least once in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.  (2) Subsection 20BK(2) and, subject to the modification in subsection (3), section 20BL, apply in relation to an initial consideration and a reconsideration under subsection (1).  (3) For the purposes of applying section 20BL, subsection 20BL(1) has effect as if the reference in that subsection to subsection 20BK(1) were a reference to subsection (1) of this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a658a29dc855dbdb0bd5b4caadf61ab5d69b461969fd7bc195b5f3632543ed44" ;
    cof:pageNumber "317"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bn-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bn-ss-2 ;
